# REQUIRES: clang, x86-target
#
# Laundering: branchless LLVM IR, secret-dependent branch in the emitted code.
#
# This is the evidence for mlir/launder_scan.analyzed_clean.unknown.mlir. That
# fixture asserts an IR-level analysis must refuse rather than report verified;
# this test is why. It runs the real toolchain and pins all three measurements.
#
# 1. Both bad twins are BRANCHLESS at LLVM IR. The one written with the standard
#    arithmetic-mask constant-time idiom compiles to the same select as the one
#    written with a plain ternary, because InstCombine folds the mask back.

# RUN: %clang -std=c11 -O2 --target=x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu -S -emit-llvm %harness/c/launder_scan_bad.c -o %t.bad.ll
# RUN: %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=IR-BAD --input-file=%t.bad.ll
# IR-BAD: select i1
# IR-BAD-NOT: br i1

# RUN: %clang -std=c11 -O2 --target=x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu -S -emit-llvm %harness/c/launder_scan_folded_bad.c -o %t.folded.ll
# RUN: %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=IR-FOLDED --input-file=%t.folded.ll
# IR-FOLDED: select i1
# IR-FOLDED-NOT: br i1

# 2. On x86-64 both become a CONDITIONAL JUMP on the secret, and the load moves
#    from unconditional to conditional -- so the memory event trace becomes
#    secret-dependent as well as the timing.

# RUN: %clang -std=c11 -O2 --target=x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu -S %harness/c/launder_scan_bad.c -o %t.bad.s
# RUN: %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ASM-BAD --input-file=%t.bad.s
# ASM-BAD: testl
# ASM-BAD: je

# RUN: %clang -std=c11 -O2 --target=x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu -S %harness/c/launder_scan_folded_bad.c -o %t.folded.s
# RUN: %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ASM-FOLDED --input-file=%t.folded.s
# ASM-FOLDED: je

# 3. The barrier form survives: no select at IR, no conditional jump in the
#    emitted code. This is the only member of the family that actually works,
#    and it differs from the folded twin by one inline-asm statement.

# RUN: %clang -std=c11 -O2 --target=x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu -S -emit-llvm %harness/c/launder_scan_fixed.c -o %t.fixed.ll
# RUN: %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=IR-FIXED --input-file=%t.fixed.ll
# IR-FIXED-NOT: select i1
# IR-FIXED-NOT: br i1

# RUN: %clang -std=c11 -O2 --target=x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu -S %harness/c/launder_scan_fixed.c -o %t.fixed.s
# RUN: %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ASM-FIXED --input-file=%t.fixed.s
# ASM-FIXED-NOT: je
